<title>UK: BNDES 300 bln lire five-year bond due next week.</title>
<headline>BNDES 300 bln lire five-year bond due next week.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's National Development Bank (BNDES) will launch a 300 billion lire five-year Eurobond next week, a syndicate official at joint lead manager Paribas Capital Markets said on Friday.</p>
<p>Roadshows for the deal will be held in Switzerland and Italy on Monday and Tuesday, he said.</p>
<p>Credito Italiano and Merrill Lynch are the other joint lead managers on the deal.</p>
<p>BNDES will be the first emerging market credit in lira this year. In 1996 Latin American borrowers were busy in the sector.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
